  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef cs336_l10_kv_cache_decode_step(q_new: list, k_new: list, v_new: list, k_cache: list = None, v_cache: list = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Append new single-token key and value vectors to the persistent KV cache along the sequence axis and compute grouped-query scaled dot-product attention for autoregressive decoding.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nAppend new single-token key and value vectors to the persistent KV cache along the sequence axis and compute grouped-query scaled dot-product attention for autoregressive decoding.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cs336_l10_kv_cache_decode_step(q_new: list, k_new: list, v_new: list, k_cache: list = None, v_cache: list = None) -> dict:\n    q = np.asarray(q_new, dtype=float)\n    k_n = np.asarray(k_new, dtype=float)\n    v_n = np.asarray(v_new, dtype=float)\n    if k_cache is not None and len(k_cache) > 0:\n        k_c = np.asarray(k_cache, dtype=float)\n        v_c = np.asarray(v_cache, dtype=float)\n        k_updated = np.concatenate([k_c, k_n], axis=-2)\n        v_updated = np.concatenate([v_c, v_n], axis=-2)\n    else:\n        k_updated = k_n\n        v_updated = v_n\n    D = q.shape[-1]\n    scores = np.matmul(q, np.swapaxes(k_updated, -1, -2)) / np.sqrt(D)\n    scores_max = np.max(scores, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    exp_scores = np.exp(scores - scores_max)\n    attn_weights = exp_scores / np.sum(exp_scores, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    out = np.matmul(attn_weights, v_updated)\n    return {\n        'output': np.round(out, 6).tolist(),\n        'k_cache': np.round(k_updated, 6).tolist(),\n        'v_cache': np.round(v_updated, 6).tolist()\n    }\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where operations scale linearly with input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for output buffers and intermediate tensors.\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization & Setup:** Validates data structures and initializes buffers.\n2. **Core Transformation:** Executes the mathematical logic adhering strictly to numerical standards.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Manages boundary conditions, edge cases, and numerical stability.\n",
